@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About — Vinyl Vault</PageTitle>

<section class="section about-hero">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="is-flex is-justify-content-space-between is-align-items-center is-flex-wrap-wrap gap-md">
            <div>
                <h1 class="about-hero-title">Vinyl Vault</h1>
                <p class="about-hero-subtitle">
                    A full-stack record shop inventory app built with Blazor, ASP.NET Core, Entity Framework Core, SQL Server, and an in-progress Azure AI catalogue assistant.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="field is-grouped is-grouped-multiline">
                <div class="control">
                    <span class="custom-badge badge-dark">Portfolio Project</span>
                </div>
                <div class="control">
                    <span class="custom-badge badge-light">Blazor</span>
                </div>
                <div class="control">
                    <span class="custom-badge badge-light">ASP.NET Core</span>
                </div>
                <div class="control">
                    <span class="custom-badge badge-light">Azure AI</span>
                </div>
                <div class="control">
                    <span class="custom-badge badge-light">SQL Server</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="container about-body">

    <div class="columns section-row">
        <div class="column is-4">
            <h2 class="row-label">System Overview</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="column is-8">
            <p class="overview-text">
                Vinyl Vault demonstrates a full-stack .NET workflow: a component-based Blazor frontend communicates with an ASP.NET Core Web API over HTTP/JSON, while Entity Framework Core manages SQL Server persistence. The system supports catalogue browsing, search, album detail views, stock visibility, and CRUD operations for record inventory. It also includes an in-progress AI assistant feature, currently wired through a mock service while Azure AI integration is being developed.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="section-divider" />

    <div class="columns section-row">
        <div class="column is-4">
            <h2 class="row-label">Architecture Stack</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="column is-8">
            <div class="columns">
                <div class="column is-6">
                    <div class="tech-card card-primary">
                        <h3 class="tech-card-title">Frontend</h3>
                        <ul class="tech-list">
                            <li>
                                <strong>Blazor Components:</strong> Reusable elements for record lists, summary cards, detail forms, and add-record workflows.
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <strong>Routing:</strong> Route-based pages for home, all records, individual record details, and adding new records.
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <strong>REST Integration:</strong> Uses HttpClient to load, create, update, and delete records through the backend API.
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <strong>Responsive UI:</strong> Styled with Bulma CSS for clean layouts across list, form, and detail pages.
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="column is-6">
                    <div class="tech-card card-secondary">
                        <h3 class="tech-card-title">Backend</h3>
                        <ul class="tech-list">
                            <li>
                                <strong>ASP.NET Core API:</strong> Exposes endpoints for browsing, searching, creating, updating, and deleting album records.
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <strong>Entity Framework Core:</strong> Uses EF Core with SQL Server for album persistence and database migrations.
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <strong>Layered Architecture:</strong> Separated controller, service, and repository structures built via dependency injection.
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <strong>Testing:</strong> Native NUnit and Moq tests safeguarding execution integrity across all layers.
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="section-divider" />

    <div class="columns section-row">
        <div class="column is-4">
            <h2 class="row-label">Data Flow</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="column is-8">
            <div class="flow-diagram">
                Blazor UI ──[HTTP / JSON]──> API Controllers ──> Services ──> Repositories ──> SQL Server
            </div>

            <p class="body-copy">
                User actions in the Blazor frontend trigger asynchronous HTTP requests to the ASP.NET Core API.
                Controllers handle routing and validation, services coordinate application logic, and repositories use
                Entity Framework Core to read and write album data in SQL Server.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="section-divider" />

    <div class="columns section-row">
        <div class="column is-4">
            <h2 class="row-label">Development Roadmap</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="column is-8">
            <div class="roadmap-list">

                <div class="roadmap-item">
                    <span class="status-badge status-blue">In Progress</span>
                    <div>
                        <strong class="roadmap-title">AI Catalogue Assistant</strong>
                        <p class="body-copy-sm">
                            Build a chat assistant for catalogue questions, album recommendations, and stock-related queries. The current version uses a mock service while Azure AI integration is being developed.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="roadmap-item">
                    <span class="status-badge status-amber">Next</span>
                    <div>
                        <strong class="roadmap-title">Authentication and Role-Based Access</strong>
                        <p class="body-copy-sm">
                            Add login, authentication, and staff-only permissions so inventory actions such as adding, updating, and deleting records are protected.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="roadmap-item">
                    <span class="status-badge status-gray">Later</span>
                    <div>
                        <strong class="roadmap-title">Image Uploads and Cloud Storage</strong>
                        <p class="body-copy-sm">
                            Replace manually entered image URLs with file uploads, storing album artwork through a managed storage service.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

   